   workB2b: {
-    'case-header-h1': 'An Interface That Didn’t Speak the User’s Language',
-    'case-header-p': 'Customers were bypassing the SaaS system and going straight to the CS team, because they couldn’t track request status, couldn’t find how to submit a new content request, and didn’t know how to communicate with the team inside the system. I identified the friction points and led four product solutions.',
-    'b2b-hero-h1': 'Identifying Friction Points and Improving UX',
-    'b2b-hero-p': 'A digital marketing platform for small and medium businesses. Identifying patterns of customers bypassing the system, and solutions that reduced friction and improved the user experience.',
-    'b2b-disclaimer-top': 'This project was carried out in a real, live work environment. The screens shown here are schematic wireframes — the company’s internal interface cannot be disclosed.',
-
-    'b2b-eyebrow-01': '01 · Context',
-    'b2b-h2-01': 'My Role',
-    'b2b-body-01': "In my role at a B2B startup, I worked across both Creative and Customer Success. On the CS side, that meant day-to-day work with the platform on behalf of subscribers: helping with the interface, running usage walkthroughs, onboarding new subscribers, and more. The technical build itself was handled by the development team. I analyzed customer calls, support tickets, and live onboarding sessions to surface friction points among small and medium business owners. Alongside this, I also created visual content for businesses across different industries, from beauty and self-care to doctors, coaches and therapists, lawyers, and more, content built for digital platforms, including posts, landing pages, and brand websites. This case study focuses on the pain points and solutions that stood out most in subscribers' everyday use of the system.",
-    'b2b-card1-title': 'Discovery calls',
-    'b2b-card1-desc': "A business discovery call with a client, to ground thinking around message-market fit",
-    'b2b-card2-title': 'Live onboarding sessions',
-    'b2b-card2-desc': 'Revealed in real time exactly where customers were getting stuck',
-    'b2b-card3-title': 'Inbound requests',
-    'b2b-card3-desc': 'Revealed recurring patterns: the same questions, the same frustrations',
-
-    'b2b-eyebrow-02': '02 · The Problem',
-    'b2b-h2-02': 'Customers Were Bypassing the System',
-    'b2b-problem-1': "Didn't understand the status of their content request to the creative team",
-    'b2b-problem-2': "Had no way to submit a new content request through the interface",
-    'b2b-problem-3': "Couldn't answer in depth during the real-time discovery call",
-    'b2b-problem-4': "Didn't know how to communicate with the team through the in-app chat",
-    'b2b-quote-02': 'Instead of using the platform, they bypassed it, creating unnecessary load on the team and hurting the user experience.',
-
-    'b2b-think-label': 'Thought Process',
-    'b2b-think-1': "In a fast-paced startup environment, I chose a lightweight, real-data-driven approach over a formal user journey mapping process or polished wireframes. I identified recurring patterns directly from customer calls and inquiries, and drafted a solution direction in writing that was reviewed with the development team before moving forward.",
-    'b2b-think-2': "The guiding logic stayed consistent across every solution. In most cases, customers weren't bypassing the system because they preferred other tools. They did it because the system didn't give them a visible or accessible enough answer. So every solution was first tested against this question: does it keep the customer inside the interface, instead of pushing them out of it.",
-    'b2b-think-3': "Decisions also kept evolving based on real user response. The content-request button, for example, was evaluated with subscribers after launch, and since the feedback showed the process was too long, it was later streamlined into a simpler, shorter flow.",
-    'b2b-think-4': "Each solution was handled independently, based on the situation at the time, rather than planned upfront as one unified initiative, but all of them stemmed from the same working hypothesis.",
-    'b2b-sketch-text': 'Wireframe sketch<br>available in the Figma project file',
-
-    'b2b-summary-h2': 'All the Changes at a Glance',
-    'b2b-summary-p': 'A summary of the solutions. Scroll down for the full breakdown of each one.',
-    'b2b-summary-img-alt': 'Full home screen of the platform',
-    'b2b-badge-1': '✓ Submit a request in one click',
-    'b2b-badge-2': '✓ Status visible on every card',
-    'b2b-badge-3': '✓ Submit an edit request from the content card',
-    'b2b-badge-4': '○ Plus button moved here',
-    'b2b-badge-5': '○ Quick access to team chat from the dashboard',
-
-    'b2b-eyebrow-sol1': '03 · Solution 1 / 4',
-    'b2b-status-implemented': '✓ Implemented',
-    'b2b-sol1-h2': 'Streamlining Content Request Tracking',
-    'b2b-sol1-quote': "The customer didn't reach out because they didn't understand. They reached out because they couldn't see.",
-    'b2b-sol1-body': "Customers had no visibility into what was happening with the request they'd submitted to the creative team, and this lack of transparency created anxiety and repeat inquiries to the CS team. A clear status view was added directly in the interface.",
-    'b2b-sol1-before-alt': 'Before screen: streamlining content request tracking',
-    'b2b-sol1-after-alt': 'After screen: streamlining content request tracking',
-    'b2b-sol1-stat': 'Repeat inquiries about request status dropped by roughly 20% after implementation.',
-
-    'b2b-eyebrow-sol2': '03 · Solution 2 / 4',
-    'b2b-sol2-h2': 'Improving How Content Requests Are Submitted',
-    'b2b-sol2-quote': 'When the path to an action is too long, the user gives up.',
-    'b2b-sol2-body1': '<strong style="color:#D4183D;">The problem:</strong> There was no way to submit a new request through the interface, only an edit request for existing content selected from the gallery. Subscribers who wanted something entirely new reached out over WhatsApp, which created load on the CS team, added an unnecessary step before the request reached the creative team, and at one point accounted for roughly 40% of inbound inquiries.',
-    'b2b-sol2-body2': '<strong style="color:#4F9E78;">The solution:</strong> A prominent primary button was added to the dashboard for submitting a content request digitally and independently. Every subscriber could now complete the action easily, which made them more self-sufficient and confident in the interface and reduced the load on the team. In addition, a quick option was added to submit an edit request directly from the content itself, instead of through the unintuitive "Help" button, which also cut down on the related inquiries that used to go through WhatsApp.',
-    'b2b-sol2-body3': '<strong style="color:#B5730D;">Next up:</strong> Following feedback from subscribers that the process is too long and cumbersome, it will be streamlined into a simpler, shorter flow.',
-    'b2b-flow-label-new': "New content request flow, previously missing from the interface",
-    'b2b-flow-new-1': 'Request for entirely new content',
-    'b2b-flow-new-2': 'The interface only had "Edit" for existing gallery content',
-    'b2b-flow-new-3': 'Reach out on WhatsApp',
-    'b2b-flow-new-4': 'CS routes the inquiry onward',
-    'b2b-flow-new-5': 'Handed off to the creative team',
-    'b2b-flow-note-new': 'Roughly 40% of inbound inquiries went through this flow',
-    'b2b-flow-label-edit': 'For comparison, the edit-request flow, which existed in the system but not as a direct action',
-    'b2b-flow-edit-1': 'Open existing content in the gallery',
-    'b2b-flow-edit-2': 'Tap the Help button',
-    'b2b-flow-edit-3': 'Reach out to the creative team',
-    'b2b-flow-edit-4': 'Write the request + attach images',
-    'b2b-flow-edit-5': 'Send to the team',
-    'b2b-flow-note-edit': "Images could be attached during the edit-request process; video files or documents only via WhatsApp. Here too: entering through the “Help” button isn't an intuitive place to request a content change.",
-    'b2b-sol2-cap1': 'After: new content request',
-    'b2b-sol2-cap2': 'After: quick edit request',
-    'b2b-sol2-alt1': 'After screen: new content request',
-    'b2b-sol2-alt2': 'After screen: quick edit request',
-    'b2b-sol2-stat': 'In the month the direct request button launched, roughly 13% of subscribers engaged with the action.',
-
-    'b2b-eyebrow-sol3': '03 · Solution 3 / 4',
-    'b2b-sol3-h2': 'Streamlining the Client Discovery Process',
-    'b2b-sol3-quote': 'Questions about brand identity require thought, not a quick response.',
-    'b2b-sol3-body': "The initial discovery process included complex questions about brand voice and differentiation, and required a 15–30 minute call that depended on the client's availability and openness, which often meant we got shallow answers. This hurt the accuracy of the content produced, created repeat conversations with subscribers, and drained the workflow while also causing frustration. After user research with subscribers, I converted the process into a digital form the client fills out after joining, with all the information saved to their profile.",
-    'b2b-cap-before': 'Before',
-    'b2b-sol3-alt-before': 'Before screen: streamlining the client discovery process',
-    'b2b-cap-after': 'After',
-    'b2b-sol3-alt-after': 'After screen: streamlining the client discovery process',
-    'b2b-sol3-stat': 'The move to a form created a natural filter: most clients completed the process independently, freeing up the team’s time to focus on those who genuinely needed a deeper discovery call.',
-
-    'b2b-eyebrow-sol4': '03 · Solution 4 / 4',
-    'b2b-status-proposed': 'Proposed · Awaiting prioritization',
-    'b2b-sol4-h2': 'Improving Chat Discoverability in the Interface',
-    'b2b-sol4-quote': "Customers used what felt familiar and safe. They couldn't find the interface's chat.",
-    'b2b-sol4-body': "The in-app chat existed, but no one saw it, since it was tucked away in a hidden menu, so customers reached out over WhatsApp because that's what they knew. To get customers operating within the interface, I proposed moving chat access to a prominent, familiar location. The choice of a floating position came from the fact that it's a familiar user behavior from other interfaces. There was no need to teach users a new pattern, just to lean on an intuitive process they already knew, used, and trusted.",
-    'b2b-sol4-cap1': 'Before: side menu',
-    'b2b-sol4-alt1': "The chat, hidden in the side menu",
-    'b2b-sol4-alt2': 'The existing path via the plus button',
-    'b2b-sol4-cap2': 'Before: plus button',
-    'b2b-sol4-alt3': 'New floating position for chat',
-    'b2b-sol4-goal': 'The goal: encourage customers to stay within the interface instead of switching to WhatsApp, with full documentation and better continuity for the team.',
-
-    'b2b-eyebrow-04': '04 · Outcome',
-    'b2b-h2-04': 'The Common Thread Across All Solutions',
-    'b2b-body-04': 'Some solutions were implemented in full. Others remain prioritized on the product roadmap. The single redesigned home screen simultaneously solved 3 of the 4 identified problems (request status, creating a new request, and reaching the team), demonstrating that one focused solution can replace several separate fixes.',
-    'b2b-stat1-title': 'Fewer repeat inquiries',
-    'b2b-stat1-desc': 'Reduced load on the CS team by surfacing information directly in the interface',
-    'b2b-stat2-title': 'More accurate discovery',
-    'b2b-stat2-desc': 'A digital form produced deeper answers and more genuine marketing content',
-    'b2b-stat3-title': 'Communication through the right channels',
-    'b2b-stat3-desc': 'Reduced off-platform communication, redirected back to the tools built for it',
-    'b2b-quote-04': 'Every solution was grounded in real data gathered from the field. Direct access to the customer is the right starting point for any improvement to the user experience.',
